aults_applied) exercise overlay/drift/defaults but none assert the baseline == the int-keyed built-in re-keyed to str"],"finding":"The Approach describes a parity test that pins the new str-keyed baseline `local_to_jira_priority` against `value_maps.LOCAL_PRIORITY_TO_JIRA`, but none of the three acceptance criteria cover this deliverable — leaving the key-type reconciliation (the plan's central correctness concern, since built-in is int-keyed 0–4 and config is str-keyed) without a covering criterion.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8d3169e45b1f25bf","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Priority key-type reconciliation'; Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n200b1dedc5e55fa0","priority":0.1375,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future edit to value_maps.LOCAL_PRIORITY_TO_JIRA silently diverges from config.local_to_jira_priority with no test failing"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add `test_priority_baseline_parity` to Acceptance Criteria asserting `config.local_to_jira_priority == {str(k): v for k, v in value_maps.LOCAL_PRIORITY_TO_JIRA.items()}`.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State in Scope whether doctor_mapping._offline_per_key should also exercise the new effective_priority_map resolver (per-key), or explicitly note priority is intentionally excluded from the doctor axis sweep as a soft/vocab-less axis.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.535,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["_offline_per_key calls rc.effective_status_map/effective_type_map/effective_link_map per key (doctor_mapping.py:126-129) but not effective_priority_map","_AXES tuple enumerates only status/type/link (doctor_mapping.py:263-267)","doctor_mapping already references priority_map/create_defaults as MappingLayer fields (:142-143), so it is a live axis-aware consumer","Plan 'Scope' Core/config list names only config.py, outbound_differ.py, outbound_mutation_builders.py, outbound_field_diff.py — doctor_mapping is not enumerated"],"finding":"The doctor_mapping command (src/rebar/_commands/doctor_mapping.py), a consumer OUTSIDE the rebar_reconciler artifact dir, enumerates the config-driven resolvers per project key in _offline_per_key (calls effective_status_map/effective_type_map/effective_link_map at :126-129) but the plan does not state whether the NEW effective_priority_map should join that per-key resolution sweep, leaving an unenumerated cross-dir consumer decision.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f937a425dc793d158","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan Scope section; src/rebar/_commands/doctor_mapping.py:117-132,263-267","norm_id":"n0bcbbcd1f5cfa47f","priority":0.165,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator runs `rebar doctor` mapping checks; a project with an unresolvable priority_map overlay would raise MappingConfigError at sync time but is not surfaced by the offline per-key resolver sweep"],"severity":"minor","sugge